---
title: The 1000 problem puzzle
excerpt: What's not to like about puzzles?
date: 2024-01-08
tags: []
---
Over the holiday period, I discovered I really like puzzles. This was initially a shock but what's not to like about puzzles. They are a box full of problems with a clear end goal.

Despite the clear end goal, each one of us have different ways of solving the problems that are the puzzle pieces. Most will start with the edges, to anchor the problems so they can't get free.

Others will group the same colours and patterns to make piles of pieces.

You may do things differently when doing the puzzle by yourself, but change to solve the puzzle differently when you are with others. I think you can learn alot about how you deal with problems and problem solving with puzzles.
